{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>An altar for burning incense.</b> It needed only a small amount of fire for the incense alone, and did not need to be hollow and filled with earth, as was required for the altar of burnt offering in order to keep the fire burning constantly on the earth. Rather, the fire on this altar was on its overlay, which was of gold, and since the fire was minimal, it was not enough to burn the body of the altar, which was of wood. This altar was not mentioned with the rest of the vessels in the section of תרומה, because its purpose was not to cause the El, blessed be He, to dwell among us, as was the purpose of the other vessels, as it says: ושכנתי בתוכם, ככל אשר אני מראה אותך את תבנית המשכן ואת תבנית כל כליו (Exodus 25:8–9). Nor was its purpose to bring down the appearance of His glory into the house, as in the matter of the sacrifices, as it says: ונעדתי שמה לבני ישראל (Exodus 29:43), and so Moses our master testified, saying: זה הדבר אשר צוה ה׳ תעשו, וירא אליכם כבוד ה׳ (Leviticus 9:6). Rather, the purpose of this altar was to honor the El, blessed be He, after He came to receive His people's service with favor — the morning and evening sacrifices — and to entreat His presence with the incense offering, after the manner of הבו לה׳ כבוד שמו, שאו מנחה ובאו לפניו (I Chronicles 16:29)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:36.707299623Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}